{#
  The ground a Trash names, inside every Trash form (the queue card, a route
  correction, a route proposal). Spam tells the rider nothing, as DSA
  Article 17(2) allows for deceptive high-volume commercial content; abuse
  sends them a statement of reasons with the facts written here, so the
  facts box is for abuse only. The server refuses abuse without facts and a
  Trash without a ground (ModerationService::trashFacts()).

  Expects `uid`, a string that keeps the ids on one page apart.

  @see docs/specs/content-reports.md §7
#}
<fieldset class="q-act-ground">
  <legend>{{ 'dsa_statement.desk.trash_ground'|trans }}</legend>
  <label><input type="radio" name="ground" value="spam" required> <span>{{ 'dsa_statement.desk.trash_spam'|trans }}</span></label>
  <label><input type="radio" name="ground" value="abuse" required> <span>{{ 'dsa_statement.desk.trash_abuse'|trans }}</span></label>
  <label for="trash-facts-{{ uid }}">{{ 'dsa_statement.desk.trash_facts'|trans }}</label>
  <textarea id="trash-facts-{{ uid }}" name="facts" maxlength="2000" rows="2"></textarea>
</fieldset>
